{
    "background_story": "Treasure was a majestic Belgian draft horse with a coat as white as freshly fallen snow. She was named after the intricate lace patterns of Valenciennes, which her owner, a skilled weaver, admired for their beauty and delicacy. Treasure's gentle giant nature made her a favorite among the farmhands, who would often take her on leisurely rides through the rolling countryside. Her calm demeanor and sure-footedness made her the perfect companion for the farm's elderly owner, who would ride her to the nearby village to deliver fresh produce. Treasure's strength and endurance were matched only by her affectionate nature, earning her a special place in the hearts of all who knew her. As she plodded along the cobblestone streets, her Valenciennes namesake seemed fitting, for she was a treasure indeed.",
